{"duration_api_ms":103739,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"39ad751e-53b7-4302-b32e-189157dabcf8","total_cost_usd":0.6830995999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":43895,"cache_read_input_tokens":812578,"output_tokens":8466,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":827},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":43895,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":76008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":8466,"cacheReadInputTokens":812578,"cacheCreationInputTokens":43895,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6830995999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":827,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":43895,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the round 2 diagnosis for sdkjs-common. The verdict changes from **refactor** to **keep**: the round 1 changes are correct, but none of them made anything faster for users that I could measure.\n\n**What I measured** (the numbers are in `.theseus/oracle/rounds/sdkjs-common-r2.md`):\n- **Unit tests:** all 7 suites pass, 10341 of 10341 assertions.\n- **Comparison against the original sdkjs:** passes on all 3 sample documents. The document content, what each user sees, the reopened file and the converted file are identical. I ran it 4 times and one run crashed in `run.cjs`; the rerun passed. So the script is a bit flaky.\n- **Timings:** the same build's times move 20–40 % from one run to the next on this VM. The original and new builds differ by less than that, and which one is faster changes from run to run.\n\n**Why keep:**\n- **PKT-0078** cut its own code path by 88 ms, but whole-document open did not get faster.\n- **PKT-0084** cut its function from 20–35 ms to under 6 ms; open time stayed within noise.\n- **PKT-0085** was never measured.\n- **What's left in common is spread thin.** No font or drawing function takes more than 31 ms on its own, and the font cache hits 98–99 % of the time. Round 1's own rule was to drop to keep if nothing was worth more than 50 ms, and that is now the case.\n- **The large cost that remains belongs to other modules.** Re-measuring text in spreadsheets during co-editing costs about 200–250 ms per 20 changes, but that code is in sdkjs-cell. The cost of applying Word co-edits belongs to sdkjs-word.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- The plan for next round is empty, since keep means no packets. The diagnosis lists what would bring back refactor: a profile on real documents or a quiet machine showing a common function group above 50 ms, or a 10-run median showing PKT-0078 or PKT-0085 saving at least 100 ms of open.\n- I did not re-run `profile-client.js`. It only profiles the bundles installed on the server, which don't contain the round 1 changes, so it can't compare original against new.\n- There was no `DIAG-sdkjs-common-b.md` to remove, and I didn't request any follow-up packets.\n\nAll 9 acceptance commands pass and `theseus scope-check` reports no files outside the target. The Executor log and the friction line are written, and everything is committed as `2c9ee86`.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- The comparison script times each case once. On this 2-CPU VM that can't show gains under about a second, so it needs a mode that takes the median of several runs.\n- None of the perf scripts measures the fork build, so improvements to sdkjs can't be proven end to end yet.","ttft_ms":6410,"type":"result","duration_ms":950880,"uuid":"2df53004-c7d2-403f-84c7-58e286b183d7","ttft_stream_ms":5100,"time_to_request_ms":463,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":261,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":15,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":4,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":41,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":11,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":6,"request_build":20},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":290,"time_to_request_major_faults":3,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":137,"process_rss_mib_result":224,"process_anon_mib_result":134,"process_peak_rss_mib":272,"process_cpu_ms_turn":15392,"process_wall_ms_turn":950879,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1305,"process_wall_ms_streaming":70210,"main_stream_count":13,"main_stream_event_count":1317,"main_stream_chunk_count":952,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1305,"wall_ms":70210,"entries":13},"tool":{"cpu_ms":12771,"wall_ms":846226,"entries":12},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":660,"wall_ms":33396,"entries":13},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":290,"wall_ms":463,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":349,"wall_ms":553,"entries":12},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":17,"wall_ms":31,"entries":1}},"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":